## Code Style

- All test classes must implement setUp and tearDown (balanced_xctest_lifecycle)
- All declarations must explicitly specify ACL (explicit_acl)
- Do not use implicitly unwrapped optionals
- Use Nimble operator overloads instead of free matcher functions
- All classes must have an explicit deinit (required_deinit)
- Do not use magic numbers — extract to constants
- Closure body must not exceed 30 lines (closure_body_length)
- Do not use async without await
- For generated SwiftGen localization files, the absence of explicit ACL and other violations is allowed if it is required for the correct operation of SwiftGen and does not interfere with the build.
- Protocols are named with the suffix -ing (for example, ClipboardManaging, ProcessingManaging) for DI-friendly architecture.
- All managers are injected through protocols for testability.
- shorthand_optional_binding: guard let self or guard let self = self is prohibited, use only guard self != nil
- public declarations must have documentation (missing_docs)
- no magic numbers: use named constants (no_magic_numbers)
- all classes must have an explicit deinit (required_deinit)
- all declarations must have an explicit ACL (explicit_acl)
- only one declaration per file (one_declaration_per_file)
- unused parameters must be removed or replaced with _ (unused_parameter)
- prefer Nimble matchers over XCTAssert (prefer_nimble)
- static instead of class in final class (static_over_final_class)
- do not use async without await (async_without_await)
- prefer non-optional Data(_:) for String->Data (non_optional_string_data_conversion)
- async_let_with_taskgroup: не использовать async let внутри withTaskGroup
- callback_to_async: для callback-based API использовать async-обёртку через withCheckedThrowingContinuation
- redundant_self_in_closure: в замыканиях не использовать self, если это не требуется
- self_binding: не использовать guard let self без присваивания
- async_without_await: не использовать async let без await

